{"name":"Enigmatic","hex":"#7e7275","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"enigmatic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to an enigma.","Mysterious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enigmatic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Enigmatic (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Enigmatic is the fourth album by Czesław Niemen, released in 1970. It has been considered by some to be the best Polish rock album ever. Inspired in 1968 by Wojciech Młynarski, Niemen decided to make his new album with Polish poetry as lyrics. Recorded in 1969, the album became very popular and was awarded with a golden record in 1971. As of 2012, the album has sold in excess of 5 million copies around the world and remains very popular."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Niemen_Enigmatic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enigmatic_(album)"},{"title":"Enigmatic scale","blocks":[{"text":"The enigmatic scale is an unusual musical scale, with elements of both major and minor scales, as well as the whole-tone scale. It was originally published in a Milan journal as a musical challenge, with an invitation to harmonize it in some way."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enigmatic_scale"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Enigmatic_scale_on_C.png/500px-Enigmatic_scale_on_C.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Enigmatic_scale_on_C.png/500px-Enigmatic_scale_on_C.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Enigmatic scale on C[1] (Playⓘ)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnigmatic_scale_on_C.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Enigmatic_scale_on_C_descending.png/500px-Enigmatic_scale_on_C_descending.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Enigmatic_scale_on_C_descending.png/500px-Enigmatic_scale_on_C_descending.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Descending enigmatic scale on C[2][3] is distinguished by F♮, a lowered fourth degree. (Playⓘ)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnigmatic_scale_on_C_descending.png"}],"sounds":{"enigmatic":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_rectangle.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_rectangle.jpg","share":0.738125},{"title":"Palafitta di Polada - Enigmatic tablets","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Palafitta_di_Polada_-_Enigmatic_tablets.jpg/500px-Palafitta_di_Polada_-_Enigmatic_tablets.jpg","ratio":0.6656891495601173,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palafitta_di_Polada_-_Enigmatic_tablets.jpg","share":0.185},{"title":"An enigmatic signpost - geograph.org.uk - 6345173","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/An_enigmatic_signpost_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6345173.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_enigmatic_signpost_-_geograph.org.